{:id "0053-lab-flick"
 :title "Lab flick: 'better like this, or like this?' reads your line back two ways, and your style moves toward the one you pick"
 :lupa/deps #{"0051-lab-board" "0052-lab-dress"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "docs/product/score.md, 'How people and agents drive it', and the
        H5 result in docs/product/lab-notebook.md. People will not tune
        parameters, but they can tell which of two performances they
        prefer. On request, the lab reads the current line back twice, as
        A (your style now) and B (one step along one axis), you flick
        toward the one you like, and your style point moves (lab.learn).
        The H5 simulation says this only works when the two are easy to
        tell apart, so a pair that would look the same is never offered."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/flick.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/flick_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/learn.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/learn_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/debug.cljc"
         "test/halfahead/lab/debug_test.cljc" "public/lab/index.html"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "halfahead.lab.learn gains (existing functions unchanged):
          (skip state) -> the state asking about the next axis, with
            nothing else changed (no flick counted).
          halfahead.lab.flick (.cljc, pure): one exam, as data.
          (distinct? plan-a plan-b) -> whether two reading plans
            (lab.reading/plan) would look or sound different: the marks
            performing or their gestures differ, or the dress differs, or
            the motion parameters of their points differ by at least 10%
            in tempo or amplitude or 0.2 in overshoot.
          (offer learn-state text pace) -> {:state s :axis k :a plan :b
            plan :point-a p :point-b p}, or nil when the text is not a
            message or no axis gives a distinct pair: take (learn/pair s);
            if its two plans are not distinct, (learn/skip s) and try the
            next axis, at most four times.
          (phases offer) -> the exam's timeline in ms from its start:
            [{:phase :a :at 0 :ms da} {:phase :gap ..400} {:phase :b ..db}
            {:phase :choose ..}], da and db each the reading's length
            (stops and cues) plus 300 ms.
          (phase-at phases t) -> the phase in force at t.
          (decide offer choice) -> the learn state after choosing :a or :b
            (learn/choose on the offer's state).
          lab.main and index.html: a 'Which?' button in the bar and Ctrl+/
            start an exam on the current text (disabled with no text or
            with reduced motion; if offer gives nil a short note says
            'Nothing to compare on this line yet'). During it: a chip
            reads 'A' while A plays, 'B' while B plays, then 'A  or  B ?'
            with two buttons; the left and right arrow keys, or the
            buttons, choose; Escape cancels and changes nothing; R plays
            the pair again. Each reading plays through the lab's reading
            path with the pair's point as the style (dress included). On
            a choice the learn state is (flick/decide ...), the style
            becomes Mine at the state's point (the board's XY dot moves
            with it), and the state is remembered per viewer in
            localStorage (try/catch). The chip is an aria-live region so
            a screen reader hears 'A', 'B', 'A or B?'. window.__lab.flick()
            -> {phase axis pointA pointB flicks point} as plain data. The
            debug overlay shows 'flick 3 · asking energy · step 0.25'.
          Tests: learn/skip; distinct? for plans that differ in each way
          and for two that do not; offer skipping an axis that shows
          nothing on a bare line and returning nil for an empty one;
          phases and phase-at; decide moves the point exactly as
          learn/choose does. Property: for any text and learn state, offer
          is nil or its two plans are distinct and its points differ on
          exactly one axis.
          e2e/lab.mjs, a new step 'flick' (?debug&reveal=3): type 'I
          loooove this (honestly). But maybe not. Ship it!' and wait for
          rest; Ctrl+/: flick().phase goes a, then b, then choose (wait on
          the data, not on the clock), and the two readings ran with
          different points (pointA and pointB differ on exactly the axis
          reported); press ArrowRight: flick().flicks is 1, point equals
          pointB, and the style picker shows Mine; Ctrl+/ then Escape:
          nothing changes; four more exams always choosing the option with
          the higher energy: point.energy has not fallen; reload: the
          point and the flick count are kept. Screenshot out/lab/flick.png
          during the choose phase.
          docs/LAB.md: a section 'The flick' with the H5 numbers' lesson
          (obvious differences, few axes)."
 :acceptance
 ["flick, learn and debug tests as in the design, on both hosts"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the flick step and every existing step; `bb
   test` stays green; out/lab/flick.png for the foreman"]
 :non-goals
 ["Never start an exam unprompted; no telemetry; nothing leaves the device"
  "No change to learn's existing functions, reading, pace, marks, score,
   gestures, synth, dress, the board's pads, the renderer or the director;
   do not edit the schema"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["docs/product/score.md" "docs/product/lab-notebook.md"
           "src/halfahead/lab/learn.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/reading.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/style.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/board.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/dress.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
           "src/halfahead/lab/debug.cljc" "public/lab/index.html"
           "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
